==Trivia==
*Maneki Cat was originally unlockable via the [[Cat Beacon]] feature, for those who paid a visit to PONOS's booth at the 5th BitSummit Indie Game Festival with a smartphone that has already cleared the first chapter of [[Empire of Cats]]. It was later made obtainable through the [[What's in the Box (Event Gacha)|What's in the Box]] Event Gacha that was added in [[Version 11.0 Update|Version 11.0]] for [[Nyanko Daisensou]]'s [[Anniversary/9th Year|9th Anniversary]] event.
*Maneki Cat gets its name and design from [[wikipedia:Maneki-neko|maneki-neko]], figures of white Cats holding [[wikipedia:Koban (coin)|koban]] in a similar fashion to Maneki Cat.
*Maneki Cat was the rarest cat in the game, with only 30 people receiving it from the BitSummit event, before it became obtainable in the [[What's in the Box (Event Gacha)|What's in the Box]] Gacha.
*[[Blue Shinobi (Special Cat)|Blue Shinobi]], [[Undead Cat (Special Cat)|Undead Cat]], Maneki Cat, [[Mr. Ninja (Special Cat)|Mr. Ninja]] and [[Firecracker Cat (Special Cat)|Firecracker Cat]] are the few units that were exclusive to the [[Nyanko Daisensou]] before being added globally via gacha event.

